[candidate · 11:37] Sorry, I was getting ahead of myself — let me redo it cleanly.

Two years ago: COGS was 42% of revenue, beans were 25% of that, so beans = 0.25 × 42 = 10.5% of revenue. Everything else in COGS was 42 − 10.5 = 31.5% of revenue.

Today COGS is 58% of revenue, so the total move is 16 points of revenue.

For beans alone to explain all 16 points, beans today would need to be 10.5 + 16 = 26.5% of revenue. As a share of today's COGS, that's 26.5 ÷ 58 ≈ 46%.

